<title>USA: CBOT April volume falls 0.2 pct yr/yr to 20.15 mln.</title>
<headline>CBOT April volume falls 0.2 pct yr/yr to 20.15 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said trading volume in its futures and options totaled 20,154,516 contracts in April, down 0.2 percent from 20,191,690 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for April 1997 and percentage change followed by April 1996 volume:</p>
<p>All futures     15,404,494     + 4.2     14,784,452</p>
<p>  Agricultural   5,011,246     -19.1	6,191,345</p>
<p>  Financial     10,390,249     +21.0	8,588,893</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   4,750,022     -12.2	5,407,238</p>
<p>  Agricultural   1,364,791     -35.7	2,124,061</p>
<p>  Financial	3,385,030     + 3.1	3,282,726</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     7,519,922     +25.1	6,010,639</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 1,703,193     + 4.4	1,632,065</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes    984,361     +20.7	  815,719</p>
<p>  Wheat		567,099     -14.2	  660,722</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,780,124     -33.0	2,655,234</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,585,514     - 5.8	1,683,153</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    576,564     -12.1	  655,984</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     445,848     + 0.6	  443,408</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,566,018     +19.0	2,155,910</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   519,091     -43.2	  914,219</p>
<p>  Corn		 434,597     -54.1	  947,421</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   540,187     -17.1	  651,530</p>
<p>((DerivativesDesk 312-408-8750/Email:derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
